WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:02.640
Okay, let's get to audience questions this
week.

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:05.840
Uh, this one came in from a few people, but
I'm reading it as submitted.

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:06.840
Ricky.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:11.320
Ricky says, Hey, David, how likely is it that
Trump will not accept the 2020 election results

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:12.910
if he doesn't win this?

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:16.760
I hate to make this as a mantic thing, but
it really depends on what you mean by not

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:17.760
accept.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:21.560
Do you mean will Trump just say the results
were bogus or do you mean will Trump actually

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:27.660
activate any means he can to try to stay in
the Oval Office despite the election results

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:32.789
indicating that he has lost the election because
Trump already has not accepted a whole bunch

00:00:32.789 --> 00:00:37.190
of stuff that he's wrong about and it's had
no material importance.

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:38.190
Right.

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:43.089
What I mean by that is Trump didn't accept
that hurricane Dorian was not threatening

00:00:43.089 --> 00:00:44.089
Alabama.

00:00:44.089 --> 00:00:47.859
He used a sharpie to draw a different weather
map, but it doesn't matter that he didn't

00:00:47.859 --> 00:00:48.859
accept it.

00:00:48.859 --> 00:00:54.709
The hurricane didn't hit Alabama and actual
meteorologists knew that it wasn't going to,

00:00:54.709 --> 00:00:59.350
Trump doesn't accept that he didn't have a
record setting crowd at his inauguration back

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:03.850
in January of 2017 but it doesn't really matter.

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:12.650
Trump doesn't accept that he truly just genuinely
lost the popular vote in 2016 to Hillary Clinton.

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:17.360
And he even actually tried to act on that
by starting a voter integrity commission,

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:20.590
but the commission found nothing and was disbanded.

00:01:20.590 --> 00:01:21.590
And that's that.

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:23.979
So let's now go back to the question.

00:01:23.979 --> 00:01:29.929
Is it likely that Donald Trump is going to
say that the 2020 election was unfair if you

00:01:29.929 --> 00:01:34.020
lose it in 2020, I think there's an almost
100% certainty of that.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:35.750
And there's a few different ways that he might
approach it.

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:40.869
He might say it was voter fraud and really
he won the election.

00:01:40.869 --> 00:01:48.219
He might sort of accept the results, but say
that it was because he had the fake news media

00:01:48.219 --> 00:01:52.359
and who knows foreign countries, whatever
working against him or China or whatever the

00:01:52.359 --> 00:01:53.429
case may be.

00:01:53.429 --> 00:02:00.509
Now, will he actually attempt to use force
to retain the presidency between November,

00:02:00.509 --> 00:02:04.689
2020 and January of 2021 when the next president
would be inaugurated?

00:02:04.689 --> 00:02:05.850
I doubt it.

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:11.210
And if he does attempt it, he will not be
allowed to stay, uh, in the end.

00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:14.670
So that is my sense of it.

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:19.069
And I know that there are a lot, interestingly,
this is way more polarizing for our audience

00:02:19.069 --> 00:02:20.659
than I thought it would be.

00:02:20.659 --> 00:02:21.659
Even among the left.

00:02:21.659 --> 00:02:25.600
I mean, I know the right is half bought in
on the idea that the only way Trump could

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:28.230
lose is if there is actually some kind of
fraud.

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:31.560
And I'm not talking to them, but even within
the left, there are people who write to me

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:34.770
and they say, no, David, you, you, you're
not understanding this.

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:37.130
Trump is going to do the things.

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:38.940
Some people on the right set Obama was going
to do.

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:44.629
He will declare martial law in order to justify
staying in the Oval Office, or he will try

00:02:44.629 --> 00:02:47.950
to suspend the 2020 election altogether or
whatever.

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:52.530
I just don't see, you know, there was no chance
Barack Obama was going to do that stuff.

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:55.810
And I don't see it, uh, as something that
Donald Trump is going to do.

00:02:55.810 --> 00:02:59.990
I think the way that he will fight it is through
a propaganda war.

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:04.541
And that's, I honestly one of the big dangers
of the fake news narrative that Donald Trump

00:03:04.541 --> 00:03:09.349
has fomented over the last couple of years
we've talked about how the fake news thing

00:03:09.349 --> 00:03:16.230
has successfully sort of caught on in the
sense that now any critical report about Donald

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:20.800
Trump is very easy for Trump as to just say
it's obviously fake.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.540
These are just people trying to take down
Trump.

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:25.120
It can't possibly be true fake news, fake
news.

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:29.379
That's one negative element of Donald Trump's
successfully running this fake news campaign.

00:03:29.379 --> 00:03:35.799
The other one though is that, uh, you, you
may be priming these folks to actually accept

00:03:35.799 --> 00:03:40.730
these absolutely outrageous narratives in
2020 depending on what your election results

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:41.730
are.

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:48.000
But in the end, I don't see any way that Trump
has even a 1% chance of actually successfully

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:49.430
doing any of those things.

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:53.000
And quite frankly, I think we need to be focused
on winning the election and getting the vote

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.000
out.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:58.250
And I know we've got to fight voter disenfranchisement
and voter suppression and election fraud and

00:03:58.250 --> 00:03:59.250
foreign interference.

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:03.629
I know we've got to do that, but if we get
enough people to vote, then it's going to

00:04:03.629 --> 00:04:07.590
be much more powerful than anything that they
can do and that's where the focus should be.

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:12.099
Rather than the idea that Trump's going to
suspend the 2020 election, he will say he

00:04:12.099 --> 00:04:13.970
didn't lose fair and square.

00:04:13.970 --> 00:04:20.390
Uh, but uh, the, the margin of victory should
be and could be so big that in the end it

00:04:20.390 --> 00:04:21.320
should not really end up making a difference.

